+  // Sunshine: any absolute directory, not only the two Program Files roots.
+  //
+  // Upstream compares the preference against DIR_PROGRAM_FILES and
+  // DIR_PROGRAM_FILESX86 and returns nothing otherwise, so the preference
+  // chooses a bitness rather than a folder. The owner decided a person must be
+  // able to choose the folder, and `docs/INSTALLER_CHOICE_PLAN.md` is what that
+  // costs. This is the whole of the change: the pipeline from a preference file
+  // to an install target already existed.
+  //
+  // **What upstream's comparison also guaranteed is gone, and that is the
+  // decision rather than an oversight.** Restricting a per-machine install to
+  // %ProgramFiles% restricts it to a directory unprivileged users cannot write.
+  // Install to a user-writable folder for all users and any unprivileged
+  // account can replace the executable every other account launches. The owner
+  // chose to warn rather than refuse (plan section 7, decision 2), and the
+  // warning lives in the front-end, which is the only part of this with a
+  // window -- and it runs there **after elevation**, because a writability test
+  // performed before elevating tests the wrong token.
+  //
+  // Two properties of upstream's version are kept deliberately:
+  //
+  //   * system installs only. The early return above already does this, and
+  //     plan section 7 decision 1 keeps it: a per-user install has no upstream
+  //     hook at all, and it is the case not being built.
+  //   * the caller chooses the *root*, never the whole path.
+  //     <Company>\<Product><suffix>\Application is appended regardless, from
+  //     constants compiled into the binary, so the shape of an installation is
+  //     still Sunshine's and only its location is the user's.
+  //
+  // What is still refused: a relative path, and one reaching through a parent.
+  // Neither is a folder anyone picked from a browse dialog; both are how a
+  // string that was not picked arrives here.
+  if (!program_files_dir.IsAbsolute() || program_files_dir.ReferencesParent()) {
+    return base::FilePath();
+  }
+
+  return program_files_dir
+      .Append(install_static::GetChromeInstallSubDirectory())
+      .Append(installer::kInstallBinaryDir);
 }
 
